<p>CALL FEATURES: 2008, 2014-2019,2022: CALLABLE 11/15/07  101</p>
<p>						 DTP 2009</p>
<p>EXTRAORDINARY REDEMPTION: THE BONDS MATURING ON NOVEMBER 15 OF THE YEARS 2009 TO 2013, INCLUSIVE, ARE SUBJECT TO REDEMPTION PRIOR TO MATURITY. THE COUNTY, IN SUCH PRINCIPAL AMOUNTS AND FROM SUCH MATURITIES AS THE COUNTY SHALL DETERMINE, AND BY LOT WITHIN A MATURITY, ON DECEMBER 1, 2007, OR ANY DATE THEREAFTER, AT A REDEMPTION PRICE OF 109% OF PRINCIPAL AMOUNT REDEEMED, PLUS ACCRUED INTEREST TO THE DATE FIXED FOR REDEMPTION, UPON THE FILING WITH THE TRUSTEE BY THE CHIEF FINANCIAL OFFICER OF THE COUNTY OF NOTICE THAT AN EXTRAORDINARY REDEMPTION EVENT HAS OCCURRED.  AN EXTRAORDINARY REDEMPTION EVENT SHALL OCCUR IF AND TO THE EXTENT THAT THE COUNTY SHALL DETERMINE TO LEASE, SELL, CONVEY OR IN ANY MANNER DISPOSE OF OR ENCUMBER, OR OTHERWISE PERMIT ANY PRIVATE USE OF, THE FACILITIES, IMPROVEMENTS OR EQUIPMENT FINANCED WITH THE PRIOR BONDS, OR ANY PORTION THEREOF.</p>
<p>* - APPROXIMATE SUBJECT TO CHANGE</p>
<p>The compliance addendum MSRB Rule G-11 will apply.</p>
<p>The award is expected Thursday, May 15, 1997.</p>
<p>Delivery is expected on June 4, 1997.</p>
<p>This issue is book entry through DTC.</p>
